      "writtenOn": "2022-01-04T23:27:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tested a fuzz target locally. The `Android.bp` file for it looks like:\n```\njava_fuzz {\n    name: \"accessibility-record-fuzzer\",\n    srcs: [\n        \"**/*.java\",\n    ],\n    static_libs: [\n        \"framework\",\n        \"jazzer\",\n    ],\n    visibility: [\"//tests/AccessibilityRecordFuzzer\"],\n}\n```\nIt depends on framework, and it gives this error when compiled without java_fuzz being device supported:\n```\nerror: frameworks/base/core/tests/fuzzers/AccessibilityRecordFuzzer/java/Android.bp:24:1: dependency \"framework\" of \"accessibility-record-fuzzer\" missing variant:\n  os:linux_glibc,arch:common\navailable variants:\n  os:android,arch:common\n```",
      "parentUuid": "a5919075_e13b4e00",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 69,
        "endChar": 54
      },
